2026-08-05 09:22:00  *** PERFORMANCE DEFECT FOUND (affects every timing ever taken on this box, and any Linux box where PETSc links threaded BLAS) ***  This PETSc (Ubuntu 3.15.5) links libopenblas + libgomp. With no thread limit set, EVERY MPI rank spawns ~30 OpenBLAS/OpenMP threads. Measured: 8 ranks -> load average 205, each rank at ~690% CPU. Effect is strongly rank-dependent because OpenBLAS only multithreads above a size threshold, so it fires at LOW rank counts (large local blocks) and stays dormant at high rank counts.
2026-08-05 09:22:00  IMPACT, measured on dt_T2_fbns 10 steps at n=4: 376.66 s unpinned -> 31.93 s with OMP_NUM_THREADS=1. That is an 11.8x loss. At n=24 the same test is 8.27 s unpinned vs 8.00 s pinned, only 3.5%, which is why the T2 production run above is NOT materially contaminated and does not need redoing. The first (unpinned) scaling attempt was discarded and rerun pinned.
2026-08-05 09:22:00  RECOMMENDATION: always launch with "mpirun -x OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 -x OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1". Worth documenting in BUILDING.md for Linux; it silently makes low-rank runs an order of magnitude slower and it fakes superlinear speedup in any scaling study.
